{"name":"April Love","hex":"#8b3d2f","fetched":"2026-10-11","looked":{"definitions":[{"term":"love","whole":false,"parts":[{"part":"Noun","definitions":["A deep caring for the existence of another.","Strong affection."]},{"part":"Verb","definitions":["To have a strong affection for (someone or something).","To need, thrive on."]}],"link":"https://en.wiktionary.org/wiki/love"}],"entries":[{"title":"April Love (film)","blocks":[{"text":"April Love is a 1957 American musical film directed by Henry Levin and produced by David Weisbart, based on the novel Phantom Filly by George Agnew Chamberlain. Photographed in CinemaScope and DeLuxe Color by Wilfred M. Cline, it was the fourth most popular movie of 1957 and stars Pat Boone, Shirley Jones, Arthur O'Connell, Dolores Michaels, Matt Crowley, Jeanette Nolan and Bradford Jackson."}],"image":"https://upload.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/en/f/fa/April_Love_%28film%29.jpg?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=api&utm_content=thumbnail_unscaled","link":"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/April_Love_(film)","wikidata":"Q3795903"},{"title":"April Love (song)","blocks":[{"text":"\"April Love\" is a popular song with music by Sammy Fain and lyrics by Paul Francis Webster. It was written as the theme song for a 1957 film of the same name starring Pat Boone and Shirley Jones and directed by Henry Levin."}],"link":"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/April_Love_(song)","wikidata":"Q4782050"},{"title":"April","blocks":[{"text":"April is the fourth month of the year in the Gregorian and Julian calendars. Its length is 30 days."}],"link":"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/April","wikidata":"Q118"},{"title":"Love","blocks":[{"text":"Love encompasses a range of strong and positive emotional and mental states, from the most sublime virtue or good habit, the deepest interpersonal affection, to the simplest pleasure. An example of this range of meanings is that the love of a mother differs from the love of a spouse, which differs from the love for food. Most commonly, love refers to a feeling of strong attraction and emotional attachment."}],"link":"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Love","wikidata":"Q316"}],"images":[{"srcset":"https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/a/ac/Breviarium_Grimani_-_April.jpg/500px-Breviarium_Grimani_-_April.jpg?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=parser&utm_content=thumbnail 1x","src":"https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/a/ac/Breviarium_Grimani_-_April.jpg/500px-Breviarium_Grimani_-_April.jpg?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=parser&utm_content=thumbnail","alt":"April, Brevarium Grimani, fol. 5v (Flemish)","link":"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/File%3ABreviarium_Grimani_-_April.jpg"},{"srcset":"https://upload.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/3/36/Diamond.jpg?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=parser&utm_content=thumbnail_unscaled 1x","src":"https://upload.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/3/36/Diamond.jpg?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=parser&utm_content=thumbnail_unscaled","alt":"Faceted diamond","link":"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/File%3ADiamond.jpg"},{"srcset":"https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/a/a9/Daisy_ntgr.JPG/500px-Daisy_ntgr.JPG?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=parser&utm_content=thumbnail 1x, https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/a/a9/Daisy_ntgr.JPG/1280px-Daisy_ntgr.JPG?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=parser&utm_content=thumbnail 2x","src":"https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/a/a9/Daisy_ntgr.JPG/500px-Daisy_ntgr.JPG?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=parser&utm_content=thumbnail","alt":"Daisy flower","link":"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/File%3ADaisy_ntgr.JPG"},{"srcset":"https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/e/ee/Sweet_Pea_%2827711557850%29.jpg/500px-Sweet_Pea_%2827711557850%29.jpg?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=parser&utm_content=thumbnail 1x, https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/e/ee/Sweet_Pea_%2827711557850%29.jpg/1280px